      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    \n    // Read matrix using scanf for speed (as in original)\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i][j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Build prefix sum matrix (integral image)\n    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> ps(n + 1, std::vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j) {\n            ps[i][j] = mat[i-1][j-1] + ps[i-1][j] + ps[i][j-1] - ps[i-1][j-1];\n        }\n    }\n\n    int mxSum = INT_MIN;\n    const int limit = n - s;  // inclusive upper bound for starting indices\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int r = 0; r <= limit; ++r) {\n        for (int c = 0; c <= limit; ++c) {\n            long long sum = ps[r + s][c + s] - ps[r][c + s] - ps[r + s][c] + ps[r][c];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = static_cast<int>(sum);\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Increase thread granularity by parallelizing only the outer submatrix row loop with schedule(static) instead of collapsing both loops, reducing OpenMP task creation overhead while maintaining balanced load. This demonstrates explicit scheduling control (schedule(static)) and coarser-grained work sharing.",
  "notes": "This experiment tests the effect of coarser-grained parallelism by only parallelizing the outer loop over submatrix starting rows, with explicit static scheduling. The inner column loop runs sequentially within each thread, increasing work per OpenMP task and reducing overhead from many small iterations.",
